136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 553 0 R
/E (Traditional biometric systems, such as fingerprint scanners, have long been the industry standard. However, they possess a significant drawback: hygiene. In a post-pandemic world, a system that requires hundreds of users to touch the same sensor surface daily is considered unhygienic and a potential vector for spreading germs and viruses. Furthermore, physical sensors are prone to wear and tear over time.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 554 0 R
/E (Our project addresses these issues by implementing a Zero-Touch \(Contactless\) solution. By using facial recognition, we provide a safer, more sanitary, and more efficient alternative that maintains high security without any physical contact between the user and the hardware.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 124 0 R
/T (3. System Architecture & Working Principle)
/E (3. System Architecture & Working Principle)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 555 0 R
/E (The operation of the system is divided into three synchronized phases:)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 556 0 R
/E (Wireless Communication: The ESP32-CAM is programmed to operate as a wireless node. It captures a high-resolution image whenever a person stands before the camera and transmits this data over a local network to a central processing unit \(a laptop or server\) running a Python-based Flask server.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 557 0 R
/E (Facial Analysis: Once the Python backend receives the image, it utilizes the Face Recognition library \(built on dlib's Deep Learning models\). The system extracts unique landmarks from the face and compares them against a pre-authorized database of "Known Faces.")
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 558 0 R
/E (Real-time Processing & Feedback:)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 559 0 R
/E (If a match is found: The system identifies the individual, logs their name and exact timestamp into a CSV-based digital register, and displays a "Welcome" message on the Tkinter GUI.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 560 0 R
/E (If no match is found: The system flags an "Access Denied" alert, providing an extra layer of security against unauthorized entry.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
